  "notes": "{萌|も}える has both a traditional meaning (to sprout) and a modern slang meaning (to feel passion).\n\nUSAGE:\n1. Traditional: for plants to bud or sprout in spring\n2. Slang: to feel strong affection/enthusiasm, especially for anime characters\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{草木|くさき}→草木：14089_kusaki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{萌|も}える: plants sprout\n- {萌黄色|もえぎいろ}: fresh green color (of new leaves)\n- ⟦この→この：00962_kono⟧⟦キャラ→キャラ：08916_kyara⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{萌|も}える: to feel passion for this character\n- {萌|も}え⟦{絵|え}→絵：02613_e⟧: moe-style illustration\n\nHOMOPHONE (different kanji):\n- ⟦{燃|も}える→燃える：02312_moeru⟧: to burn (fire)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nThe slang {萌|も}え originated in ⟦オタク→オタク：15181_otaku⟧ culture and expresses affection for fictional characters.",
